, 10, 64, 1.2, 5.0),\n    (2, 128, 512, 8, 64, 1.0, 5.0),\n]\n\nseed = 17\nfor i, (B, L, C, H, D, alpha, beta) in enumerate(cases):\n    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed * 1009 + i)\n    x = torch.randn(B, L, C, generator=g)\n    wq = torch.randn(H, D, C, generator=g) / math.sqrt(C)\n    wk = torch.randn(H, D, C, generator=g) / math.sqrt(C)\n    wv = torch.randn(H, D, C, generator=g) / math.sqrt(C)\n    \n    y_cur = current(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n    y_me = mem_eff(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n    diff = (y_cur - y_me).abs().max().item()\n    \n    n = 11\n    for _ in range(3): \n        current(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        mem_eff(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n    \n    t_cur = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        current(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        t_cur.append((t1-t0)/1e6)\n    \n    t_me = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        mem_eff(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        t_me.append((t1-t0)/1e6)\n    \n    speedup = statistics.median(t_cur) / statistics.median(t_me)\n    print(f'Case {i} (B={B},L={L},C={C},H={H},a={alpha}): speedup={speedup:.3f}x  cur={statistics.median(t_cur):.2f}ms  me={statistics.median(t_me):.2f}ms  diff={diff:.1e}')\n\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"Case 0 (B=1,L=64,C=512,H=8,a=1.05): speedup=1.017x  cur=1.39ms  me=1.37ms  diff=0.0e+00\nCase 1 (B=1,L=128,C=640,H=10,a=1.1): speedup=0.974x  cur=4.62ms  me=4.74ms  diff=0.0e+00\nCase 2 (B=1,L=128,C=1280,H=20,a=1.15): speedup=1.001x  cur=14.25ms  me=14.25ms  diff=0.0e+00\nCase 3 (B=1,L=256,C=1280,H=20,a=1.05): speedup=1.011x  cur=41.93ms  me=41.48ms  diff=0.0e+00\nCase 4 (B=1,L=256,C=640,H=10,a=1.2): speedup=1.005x  cur=15.14ms  me=15.06ms  diff=0.0e+00\nCase 5 (B=2,L=128,C=512,H=8,a=1.0): speedup=0.672x  cur=4.22ms  me=6.28ms  diff=0.0e+00\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The `del` approach has inconsistent results and actually hurts case 5 significantly (probably because the alpha==1 fast path is shorter and del overhead dominates). Let me focus on more meaningful optimizations.\n\nLet me think about a completely different angle. The three linear projections are the biggest cost. What if we can compute `logits` without explicitly forming q and k?\n\n`logits = q @ k^T / sqrt(D) = (x @ wq^T) @ (x @ wk^T)^T / sqrt(D) = x @ wq^T @ wk @ x^T / sqrt(D)`\n\nWait, let me check dimensions:\n- x: (B, L, C), wq: (H, D, C), wk: (H, D, C)\n- x @ wq^T for each head... this is per-head.\n- logits[b,h,i,j] = sum_d q[b,h,i,d] * k[b,h,j,d] / sqrt(D)\n- = sum_d (sum_c x[b,i,c] * wq[h,d,c]) * (sum_c' x[b,j,c'] * wk[h,d,c']) / sqrt(D)\n- = sum_c sum_c' x[b,i,c] * x[b,j,c'] * sum_d wq[h,d,c] * wk[h,d,c'] / sqrt(D)\n- = sum_c sum_c' x[b,i,c] * K[h,c,c'] * x[b,j,c']\n\nwhere K[h,c,c'] = wq[h,:,c] @ wk[h,:,c'] / sqrt(D) = wq[h] @ wk[h]^T / sqrt(D)\n\nSo logits[b,h] = x @ K[h] @ x^T. K has shape (H, C, C).\n\nCost: K computation: H*C*C*D. For case 3: H=20, C=1280, D=64: 20*1280*1280*64 = 2.1B ops. That's a lot.\n\nBut we only need K once per call. The q+k projections cost: 2 * BL*C*HD = 2 * 256*1280*1280 = 840M ops.\n\n2.1B > 840M, so K approach is worse. Unless C is much smaller than D... but D=64, C ranges from 512-1280.\n\nLet me think about something else. What about the output projection? Can we compute `r * p_mix @ v` more efficiently?\n\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. What if we:\n1. Compute q, k, v projections (3 matmuls - unavoidable)\n2. But compute v in the same BL layout and not re-order to BH layout until needed\n3. Use 4D tensors with .view for everything\n\nWait, let me try something: since `bmm` is our workhorse, can we compute `p_mix @ v` by doing it in the `(B*L, H*D)` space somehow? No, that doesn't work because attention is per-head.\n\nLet me try one more thing: using `torch.baddbmm` for the logits:\n"}}
