{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"No significant difference. Let me try a different approach - let me think about the problem from the perspective of the reference baseline (starter) and see if there's a fundamental transformation we're missing.\n\nActually, let me explore one more idea: **computing G from q and k** — no, G = x @ x^T.\n\nLet me try another idea: what if we compute v first, then use it to compute... no, v isn't useful for anything besides the output.\n\nLet me try one more thing: **replacing permute+contiguous+view with a more efficient rearrangement**.\n\nActually, I just realized something. We currently compute q and k as (BH, L, D), then compute logits as bmm(q, k^T). But we could compute k in (BH, D, L) layout and then bmm(q, k) directly. Wait, I tried that and it was slower because the k projection then needs a different transpose.\n\nLet me think about the actual memory layout more carefully:\n- q projection: xr @ wqr.T gives (BL, HD), laid out as (L, H*D) for B=1\n- We want q as (BH, L, D) contiguous = (H, L, D) for B=1\n- View as (B, L, H, D) → permute to (B, H, L, D) → contiguous → view as (BH, L, D)\n- This does a physical copy (the contiguous call), moving 256*1280 = 328K elements per matrix\n\nIs there a way to avoid this copy? Well, `bmm` needs the 3D tensor to be... let me check if bmm can handle non-contiguous tensors:\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cd /workspace && python3 -c \\\"\nimport torch, math, time, statistics\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nHD = H * D\nBH = B * H\n\ng = torch.Generator().manual_seed(17*1009+3)\nxr = torch.randn(B*L, C, generator=g)\nwqr = torch.randn(HD, C, generator=g) / math.sqrt(C)\nwkr = torch.randn(HD, C, generator=g) / math.sqrt(C)\n\nn = 50\n\n# Approach 1: permute + contiguous + view\ndef way1():\n    q = (xr @ wqr.T).view(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous().view(BH, L, D)\n    k = (xr @ wkr.T).view(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous().view(BH, L, D)\n    return torch.bmm(q, k.transpose(1, 2))\n\n# Approach 2: transpose directly from BL,HD to BH,L,D\n# (BL, HD) = (L, H*D) for B=1. We want (H, L, D) for B=1.\n# (L, H*D) --view--> (L, H, D) --permute(1,0,2)--> (H, L, D)\n# This is the same as approach 1 essentially.\n\n# Approach 3: use as_strided? No, not contiguous.\n\n# Approach 4: can bmm work with non-contiguous last dim?\nq_nc = (xr @ wqr.T).view(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)  # non-contiguous in last dims\nk_nc = (xr @ wkr.T).view(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n# Try bmm on reshaped version\ndef way_bmm_nc():\n    q = q_nc.reshape(BH, L, D)  # this won't work if not contiguous in last dims\n    k = k_nc.reshape(BH, L, D)\n    return torch.bmm(q, k.transpose(1, 2))\n\ntry:\n    r = way_bmm_nc()\n    print(f'bmm with nc: ok, shape={r.shape}')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'bmm with nc: {e}')\n\n# Let's check if q_nc.reshape works\nprint(f'q_nc shape: {q_nc.shape}')\nprint(f'q_nc stride: {q_nc.stride()}')\ntry:\n    qr = q_nc.reshape(BH, L, D)\n    print(f'reshape works, stride: {qr.stride()}')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'reshape fails: {e}')\n\n# 4D matmul approach\ndef way_4d():\n    return q_nc @ k_nc.transpose(-1, -2)\n\nfor name, fn in [('way1 (contig bmm)', way1), ('way4 (4D matmul)', way_4d)]:\n    for _ in range(5): fn()\n    times = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        fn()\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        times.append((t1-t0)/1e6)\n    print(f'{name:25s}: median={statistics.median(times):.3f}ms')\n\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
